  "scientific_conclusion": "Calibrated HARPS_ECELLE_V3 search across 50 fresh exposures of 10 nearby solar-analog stars (15.2-46.3 pc) + 10 control exposures on 2 stars completed: prospective Gates G1-G5 reduced transient candidates on science exposures from 34 (V2) to 5 (0.10/exp vs 0.50/exp in control) while yielding 28 control (2.80/exp) vs 148 science (2.96/exp) nominal G1-G5 passers (zero science excess). Deterministic forensic vetting (Tests F1 & F2) confirms 166/166 Channel P passers are sub-continuum photospheric absorption mismatches (max fn_pk3 = 0.979 < 1.0) and 10/10 Channel T passers are oblique 2D cosmic-ray/pedestal artifacts: 0 verified ETI laser detections, setting 8-sigma upper limits of median 47.0 kW (range 17.3-201.4 kW) for a 10 m beamed transmitter across 3800-6900 A."
